From 6a56835eef73ac4f047f1c05d6b529a3503d42e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Lazarev <lazarev@tactiqedge.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:08:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] configs: rock5a-rk3588s: declare writeable environment
 variables

CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST permits writes and imports only for variables
carrying the w flag, and takes that list from the compile-time constant
ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC (env/flags.c), not from the .flags variable in the
environment, so that the access list cannot be supplied by the
environment it governs. In this version the board part of that constant
is the Kconfig string CONFIG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC (include/env_flags.h),
which defaults to an empty string: with the option enabled and no board
value, no variable is writeable and nothing is imported from the saved
environment at all.

Declare the three RAUC A/B state variables in the board defconfig, as
other boards do for the same scheme. Without them the boot_ab script
cannot decrement the try counter, automatic rollback to the other slot
never happens, and fw_setenv BOOT_ORDER has no effect after a reboot.

bootargs and bootcmd are deliberately left out: keeping them
non-importable is what prevents the kernel command line from being
changed from a running system.

The 2024.07 tree defines CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC in the board header
instead; in this version that macro is no longer read, and a board
header define is silently ignored.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on the TactiQ default environment; the variable names come from tactiq-boot.env]
---
 configs/rock5a-rk3588s_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/rock5a-rk3588s_defconfig b/configs/rock5a-rk3588s_defconfig
index 24b2eef3..78f02b4c 100644
--- a/configs/rock5a-rk3588s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/rock5a-rk3588s_defconfig
@@ -68,3 +68,4 @@ CONFIG_USB_OHCI_GENERIC=y
 CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y
 CONFIG_USB_DWC3_GENERIC=y
 CONFIG_ERRNO_STR=y
+CONFIG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC="BOOT_ORDER:sw,BOOT_A_LEFT:dw,BOOT_B_LEFT:dw"
-- 
